{"title":"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Shortcut\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Shortcut</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Another_Shortcut_(Extended_Law_of_Sines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Another Shortcut (Extended Law of Sines)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Coordinates)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Coordinates)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Heron&#39;s_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Heron's Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Symmetry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Symmetry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Similar_to_others)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Similar to others)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pyramid has a triangular base with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The three edges of the pyramid from the three corners of the base to the fourth vertex of the pyramid all have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The volume of the pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f1dcbb9badfd3447d4e7351678b7d71ea9bff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5f14d96f35589e132274f04f01d86405ffa346.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; size(200); currentprojection=orthographic(4, -2, 2); triple A = (-12, 0, 0); triple B = (12, 0, 0); triple C = (0, 16, 0); triple V = (0, 3.5, 21.65); // Height is sqrt(468.75) ≈ 21.65 draw(A--C, dashed); draw(A--B--C); draw(V--A); draw(V--B); draw(V--C); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, S); label(&quot;$V$&quot;, V, N); label(&quot;24&quot;, (A+B)/2, S); label(&quot;20&quot;, (B+C)/2, SE); label(&quot;25&quot;, (V+B)/2, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"265\" height=\"328\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the triangular base be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e4930f45cc7de56d59fc838e4ab39dca6403b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AB} = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />. We find that the altitude to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238f77f5bd36cadced68f029e4554015289e50ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AB}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a155323f6426996d0d0ff5f62e8a55b50d369415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(24*16)/2 = 192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Let the fourth vertex of the tetrahedron be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238f77f5bd36cadced68f029e4554015289e50ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AB}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> perpendicular to the plane of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> will pass through the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, which we will call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is equidistant from each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d75153decb11608d4f586ac24d9a60d5893c21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline {OM} + \\overline {OC} = \\overline {CM} = 16\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4375ac75b94beb1add31a241a62d5cafce9ee1b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {OM} = d$\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aa0ed958dd3c71f1a33a63fdba464a0bcb3e91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC=OA=\\sqrt{d^2+12^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"192\" height=\"21\" />\nEquation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/9/3d9cc1288f580a990568ba0cb0bb4318828cb8f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d + \\sqrt {d^2 + 144} = 16\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Squaring both sides, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea859648a4ef6f195715d2d6a57f2f48f921fdbc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d^2 + 144 + 2d\\sqrt {d^2+144} + d^2 = 256\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/998921352619df04b0f0c90574cdfb04d0ace04e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2d^2 + 2d\\sqrt {d^2+144} = 112\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847086f0e986167537a70e9bb66d5b265782a46a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2d(d + \\sqrt {d^2+144}) = 112\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Substituting with equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/93940860115e0385946ccc5df2741a25c4c6ad78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2d(16) = 112\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd40471f3ada8d236648bce5b2ce23c261c7471.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = 7/2\\]\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We now find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd58888a799f061abfbcb5b8d83786ee7dcd3ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{d^2 + 144} = 25/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Let the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4fad8b6a6020ce22533889eba5c727c34c754a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {OP} = h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. Using the Pythagorean Theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65d6fe768733942de7abb4a750badc3527cb5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00a3aec203d36763bff1de1788496aa77b07f34c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84614f20f337820ee6b9dd1d2f27e74e3ca80dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> (all three are congruent by SSS):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154e070cd93d97ff918ddee3bde5f29d1e41d4ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25^2 = h^2 + (25/2)^2\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/6630f7d5f5bc9509384c97ff4ff3da7331ed777b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[625 = h^2 + 625/4\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e67ccc3af31d9886eca450ef38ff0222c4bd853.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1875/4 = h^2\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d741afa2f15bdecc80e07412827ddbae8721584b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25\\sqrt {3} / 2 = h\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><br />\nFinally, by the formula for volume of a pyramid,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/c/f9cf1eea77eb1f7452e398407863e0c987f532db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = Bh/3\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb04dc15ea3ee95f66b644e5347f96692797c18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = (192)(25\\sqrt{3}/2)/3\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"21\" />\nThis simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b8620bd928f17628958073f3a5a5d29172e5236a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = 800\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea86ca9aae75c0b0d36fd895223b4752492f00c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed {803}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNOTE&#160;: If you don’t know or remember the formula for the volume of a triangular pyramid, you can derive it using calculus as follows&#160;:\n</p><p>Take a small triangular element in the pyramid. We know that it’s area is proportional to the height from the vertex to the base. Hence, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b1f8e119669e1359981f40ef538b322986a129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A_{small element}}{A} = \\frac{h^2}{H^2} \\implies A_{small element} = \\frac{Ah^2}{H^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"360\" height=\"41\" />. Now integrate it taking the limits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Shortcut\">Shortcut</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Shortcut\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Here is a shortcut for finding the radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>As before, we find that the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lands on the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da35a0d0a8952651e752f9a0afa0662c0c143b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0834a58059a61a79d86701cc1292ee73a0858c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=b$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474cd45035e0eea00cfc2d9355528e69dc34389d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=c$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\nThen we write the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> in two ways:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f6098096dca8b3d4c038af84f605e7f542664f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC]= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 24 \\cdot 16 = \\frac{abc}{4R}\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> respectively, and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe1a78d7899b997e65b280abdc226bb6d6fd31f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R= \\frac{25}{2}=OA=OB=OC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"218\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Then continue as before to use the Pythagorean Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a2e986f5740b99d5f4b55ff7c5970dca4b277a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AOP$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and find the volume of the pyramid.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Another_Shortcut_.28Extended_Law_of_Sines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Another_Shortcut_(Extended_Law_of_Sines)\">Another Shortcut (Extended Law of Sines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Another Shortcut (Extended Law of Sines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Take the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/2455cd96e48165f8fe0044c0f321897aeb72fe8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b942e2c2543e99ce5e03158682c0846d2df962.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. Draw an altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> that bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Then the altitude has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aad7e4e536ba42e87f188d1b0d2bcd406a19d3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{20^2 - 12^2} = \\sqrt{16^2} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"198\" height=\"22\" />. Next, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fff5d29d3d19a525e5bd99ab4711198058b02fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. Then from the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7a0327109ede54bf3abf9eb325bb58a503afc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c69a93db6ed448e17a88403233fc6a341d03eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = 4/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />. From the extended law of sines, the circumradius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5b5edea95cb5d32ade3d245c03db2c3a35c171a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\cdot \\dfrac{5}{4} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{25}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Coordinates.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Coordinates)\">Solution 2 (Coordinates)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Coordinates)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can place a three dimensional coordinate system on this pyramid. WLOG assume the vertex across from the line that has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is at the origin, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4e5fa16269a1c2026a4a1a9e79fc512b921dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. Then, the two other vertices can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca8960c0aaee67d612ad5052415f73a37181f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-12, -16, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c504eba701d435f35676915ce1a44ab9545f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(12, -16, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Let the fourth vertex have coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />. We have the following <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equations from the distance formula.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e255ac75e9b9df5385b1df59ea848b91cdaface.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+y^2+z^2=625\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e4bdb64cb1a4562889a811b16ab359fabe3dfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+12)^2+(y+16)^2+z^2=625\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1ff9a7552449d5257938bb5fd3bbe378ead9cd8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-12)^2+(y+16)^2+z^2=625\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Adding the last two equations and substituting in the first equation, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00ef901207e79a986c03953673c9efe0715239e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{25}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />. If you drew a good diagram, it should be obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Now, solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db7a8f7e8d1ed2cbbb0ccbe651af2fe5025a2675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"41\" />. So, the height of the pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40f2f662acf425a3fec776cc7cefab48975afde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"41\" />. The base is equal to the area of the triangle, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8efe01fbd7aef3c80516bf4d2ddd4188fc33462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 24 \\cdot 16 = 192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"126\" height=\"37\" />. The volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16ee65c55193815814976714c4a4c857469c43b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 192 \\cdot \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 800\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"189\" height=\"41\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c5439516a4bd31b5183a1a80e8f8bd1116a9ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800+3 = \\boxed{803}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><b>-RootThreeOverTwo</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Heron.27s_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Heron's_Formula)\">Solution 3 (Heron's Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Heron&#39;s Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Label the four vertices of the tetrahedron and the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238f77f5bd36cadced68f029e4554015289e50ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {AB}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, and notice that the area of the base of the tetrahedron, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b940d283ec4a89f128f2d093ce24b514ac8377d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$192$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, according to Solution 1. \n</p><p>Notice that the altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e34ee19d577da0459910e2821ffb3920d882c32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CPM$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d07966d795ff9057054da9b88741e863bf2d4864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {CM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the height of the tetrahedron. Side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eee9b0931fb73ec5162fbf200a4bd2b4c44ce64a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {PM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> is can be found using the Pythagorean Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11b53ca3801f4cd141552fbf23718266c47d382d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APM$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/8/cb82467edb99745921d98665464c9cc957d98db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {PM}=\\sqrt{481}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>Using Heron's Formula, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e34ee19d577da0459910e2821ffb3920d882c32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CPM$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> can be written as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278f3e6d616ab6099179415faa1131424b27345b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{41+\\sqrt{481}}{2}(\\frac{41+\\sqrt{481}}{2}-16)(\\frac{41+\\sqrt{481}}{2}-25)(\\frac{41+\\sqrt{481}}{2}-\\sqrt{481})}\\]\" width=\"551\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c975061310c6fd5461db407f319886c7e19c968a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{\\sqrt{(41+\\sqrt{481})(9+\\sqrt{481})(-9+\\sqrt{481})(41-\\sqrt{481})}}{4}\\]\" width=\"422\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>Notice that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/994640187877e479e8b4d661438c85c382e57594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(41+\\sqrt{481})(41-\\sqrt{481})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/6515990028f06b2243863dba505c43e47101418d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9+\\sqrt{481})(-9+\\sqrt{481})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" /> can be rewritten as differences of squares; thus, the expression can be written as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d413e5b1e6c55f1f4a28ff202d81e976e1f77b22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{(41^2-481)(481-9^2)}}{4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{480000}}{4}=100\\sqrt{3}.\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>From this, we can determine the height of both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e34ee19d577da0459910e2821ffb3920d882c32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CPM$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc36e0b024b3261941e69b9cc2eb20152b6cd4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCP$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295360fe40ea060e845488126aad0913fba8ee3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100\\sqrt{3}}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"41\" />; therefore, the volume of the tetrahedron equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/2948806e58492e230b3068d60332b65a90c39662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\cdot 192=800\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"172\" height=\"41\" />; thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b93c7d13006f5d03f24b69710f895e89617e56f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=800+3=\\boxed{803}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><b>-dzhou100</b>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Symmetry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Symmetry)\">Solution 4 (Symmetry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Symmetry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2017_AIME_I_4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b6/2017_AIME_I_4.png/450px-2017_AIME_I_4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"347\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b6/2017_AIME_I_4.png/675px-2017_AIME_I_4.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/b6/2017_AIME_I_4.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Notation is shown on diagram. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a2bfed47b3a84b5b47aee170bc898083df1caa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AM = MB = c = 12, AC = BC = b = 20,\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8edc9d260e26b415174fe2c8cd90543f006ed372.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DA = DB = DC = a = 25.\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349921f20abd693271308d0df7ba3a665b2f039f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CM = x + y = \\sqrt{b^2-c^2} = 16,\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d780f461953d318d764da0ec1522d0491769db4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 - y^2 = CD^2 – DM^2 = CD^2 – (BD^2 – BM^2) = c^2 = 144,\\]\" width=\"439\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2fdc2ba0dfd17d96bbf56719c56c1cf61bbd0ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x – y = \\frac{x^2 – y^2}{x+y} = \\frac {c^2} {16} = 9,\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc8d2544b9d17ed647344f62648b8d7a8a338b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac {16 + 9}{2} = \\frac {a}{2},\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f95dae6594f1bedb956bd3d97396dd231433a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h = \\sqrt{a^2 -\\frac{ a^2}{4}} = a \\frac {\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec04c83ed61bcd4eecbec1d9ce7b19fa9998243.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = \\frac{h\\cdot CM \\cdot c}{3}= \\frac{16\\cdot 25 \\sqrt{3} \\cdot 12}{3} = 800 \\sqrt{3} \\implies \\boxed {803}.\\]\" width=\"421\" height=\"41\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Similar_to_others.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Similar_to_others)\">Solution 5 (Similar to others)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Similar to others)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Fact 1:</b>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumsphere of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><b>Lemma:</b>\n</p><p>The altitude of the tetrahedron from apex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> intersects plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> at the circumcentre.\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma:</b>\n</p><p>The horizontal plane that passes through any part of the sphere always maps a perfect circle, so the horizontal plane that passes through triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> passes through a circle. The diameter of the sphere perpendicular to the plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has the property that it will always be located at the centre of any given plane. Therefore, say this line intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the centre of the circle that passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, and therefore the circumcentre.\n</p><p><b>2017 AIME I Q4:</b>\n</p><p>Through simple formulae the circumradius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d74e82f3b7ff8814639fa300e287c601edf9af4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the triangle containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/0448207f3062fba301e810680f612e359a51c623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is 30-60-90 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df908604c184d1f2540379b2c55f08d1b96f0bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO = \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"43\" />. From there, the area of the base triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is 192, so we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c269d49fa848f9f772868ee2b4f7a4adf5906f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 \\cdot 25\\sqrt{3} = 800\\sqrt{3} \\implies \\boxed{803}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"239\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Mk-MCeVjSGc\">https://youtu.be/Mk-MCeVjSGc</a>\n~Shreyas S\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I\" title=\"2017 AIME I\">2017 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\